Revision: 541566932abbaebcb0a40e562a1f846738383f38

What was changed in the Fish Audio Materials:
  - Import paths were changed from fish_speech.* to red_curtain.*.
  - generate_drama3() in fish_omni/generate.py got a progress callback and a
    cancel/safety callback that is checked between model steps.
  - Nothing else in fish_omni/ was modified. The original CUDA / FP8 path is
    still in the files but is not called on ROCm.

New code that works with the Fish Audio Materials (in red_curtain/, MIT):
  - adapter.py loads the checkpoint itself: dense weights go to the GPU in
    BF16, the block-FP8 MoE experts stay compressed in system RAM.
  - memory.py replaces the NVIDIA FP8 GEMM with FP8 block dequantization plus
    a regular PyTorch matmul, and keeps recently used experts in a bounded
    LRU cache on the GPU.
  - residency.py moves the backbone and audio decoder to system RAM while the
    DAC decodes, and back for the next generation.

